# Each phrase announces that the writer is about to say a thing again.
# The fix keeps the clearer of the two statements, and deletes both the
# other one and the phrase. `in other words` counts only with a glued
# comma, because the bare form ends a clause (`restates it in other
# words`). `put differently`, `said differently`, `stated differently`,
# and `to put it another way` need the comma too. `That is,` stays out,
# because the Latin-abbreviation rule offers it as the fix for `i.e.`.
# `to be clear` also needs the start of a clause after its comma,
# because the infinitive takes a list of adjectives (`comments to be
# clear, accurate, and readable`). A comma ends Harper's default chunk,
# so the rule reads whole sentences to see past it.
#
# A summary opener (`In summary,`, `In conclusion,`, `To sum up,`)
# announces that the paragraph is about to say its point again. It
# counts here too, with the glued comma of an opener. The fix moves a
# closing summary to the start, where it tells the reader what the
# paragraph shows. The Recommended rule of the same name holds the
# openers that also lead a new point (`In short,`, `Ultimately,`).
#
# `put simply` and `to put it simply` sit in the minimizer rule, which
# reports every `simply` but the one before `put`, so each set of words
# draws one finding.
#
# It hit 77 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 20 of 20 sampled hits
# opened a restatement or a summary.
expr main [(in other words,), (simply put), (that is to say), (to be clear, [DET, PRON, PROPN, NOUN]), (in summary,), (in conclusion,), (to sum up,), (to summarize,), (all in all,), (put differently,), (said differently,), (stated differently,), (to put it another way,)]
let message "Restatement. Keep the clearer of the two statements, and delete the other one and the phrase. Move a closing summary to the start."
let description "Flags phrases that announce the writer is about to say a thing again."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
let scope "Sentence"
allows "The summary restates the claim in other words."
allows "Rewrite the comments to be clear, accurate, and readable."
